{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.4ff34dbbf6","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-c-391","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>The Quarry Observatory is in northern Chile. It began operating in 2015.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 8 meters.</li><li>The Sable Observatory is in western Kenya. It began operating in 1955.</li><li>Its main telescope's mirror diameter is 6 meters.</li><li>Both are radio observatories.</li></ul><p>The student wants to contrast the locations of the two observatorys.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["The Quarry Observatory, which is in northern Chile, is one of several radio observatories.","The Quarry Observatory began operating in 2015, while the Sable Observatory began operating in 1955.","The main telescope's mirror diameter of the Quarry Observatory (8 meters) is greater than that of the Sable Observatory (6 meters).","The Quarry Observatory is in northern Chile, and the Sable Observatory is in western Kenya."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal asks for a specific kind of comparison. It names where both are and contrasts them. The other choices compare dates or size, or mention only one location."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.1e86686cfd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-13","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Castellano is a psychologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether taking short breaks improves students' focus during long study sessions.</li><li>Castellano had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.</li><li>Castellano found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.</li><li>Castellano concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Castellano had one group of students take a five-minute break every half hour while another group studied without breaks.","Castellano found that students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly.","Because students who took breaks answered more practice questions correctly, Castellano concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused.","Castellano concluded that brief breaks may help people stay focused."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.64251b1ab5","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-19","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Halvorsen is an agricultural scientist.</li><li>Halvorsen wanted to find out whether planting clover between rows of corn reduces the need for fertilizer.</li><li>Halvorsen grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons.</li><li>Halvorsen found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.</li><li>Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer, Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","Halvorsen found that fields with clover produced similar yields using a third less fertilizer.","Halvorsen concluded that clover may supply some of the nutrients corn needs.","To investigate the question, Halvorsen grew corn with and without clover planted between the rows for three seasons."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.4aa1bc2b7b","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-29","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Tomás Varga is a materials scientist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether a coating made from seaweed can keep fruit fresh longer.</li><li>Varga coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.</li><li>Varga found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.</li><li>Varga concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste.","Varga found that coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer.","To investigate the question, Varga coated half of a batch of strawberries with a seaweed-based film and left the rest uncoated.","Because coated strawberries stayed fresh for about four days longer, Varga concluded that the coating could help reduce food waste."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.94a11e97bd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-45","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kwame Delacroix is a geologist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether a hillside's plant cover affects how much soil washes away in heavy rain.</li><li>Delacroix measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses.</li><li>Delacroix found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","Because bare slopes lost several times more soil, Delacroix concluded that plant cover may protect hillsides from erosion.","Delacroix found that bare slopes lost several times more soil.","To investigate the question, Delacroix measured soil runoff on bare slopes and on slopes covered with native grasses."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.7a7583900d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-49","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Asante is a nutrition researcher.</li><li>Asante wanted to find out whether eating breakfast affects how much food people eat at lunch.</li><li>Asante asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.</li><li>Asante found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.</li><li>Asante concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Asante asked volunteers to eat breakfast on some days and skip it on others, then measured their lunch portions.","Because lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days, Asante concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later.","Asante found that lunch portions were about the same on both kinds of days.","Asante concluded that skipping breakfast may not lead people to eat more later."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.355fbeb024","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-65","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Castellano is an astronomer.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether a distant star's brightness changes on a regular schedule.</li><li>Castellano measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.</li><li>Castellano found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.</li><li>Castellano concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days, Castellano concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star.","Castellano found that the star dimmed slightly about every 42 days.","To investigate the question, Castellano measured the star's brightness every night for eighteen months.","Castellano concluded that an orbiting planet may be passing in front of the star."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.6c197e154f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-70","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Takeda is a linguist.</li><li>Takeda wanted to find out whether bilingual children are better at switching between tasks.</li><li>Takeda gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.</li><li>Takeda found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors.</li><li>Takeda concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors, Takeda concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","Takeda concluded that speaking two languages may strengthen certain mental skills.","To investigate the question, Takeda gave bilingual and monolingual children a game that required switching rules quickly.","Takeda found that bilingual children switched rules with fewer errors."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.e9101df83f","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-78","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ayumi Abara is a botanist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Abara grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Abara found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Abara concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","To investigate the question, Abara grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.","Because plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates, Abara concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Abara found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.f748c13b0d","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-83","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Nakamura is a botanist.</li><li>Nakamura wanted to find out whether tomato plants grow better with music played nearby.</li><li>Nakamura grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without.</li><li>Nakamura found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.</li><li>Nakamura concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates, Nakamura concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","Nakamura found that plants in both greenhouses grew at similar rates.","Nakamura concluded that music may have little effect on tomato growth.","To investigate the question, Nakamura grew tomato plants in two identical greenhouses, one with music and one without."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.894b15c5bd","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-86","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Idris Oyelaran is an urban planner.</li><li>Oyelaran wanted to find out whether adding trees along streets lowers summer temperatures.</li><li>Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover.</li><li>Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.</li><li>Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Because streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler, Oyelaran concluded that street trees may help cities stay cooler in summer.","Oyelaran found that streets with trees were up to four degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Oyelaran measured afternoon temperatures on streets with and without tree cover."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.26825fd11c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-92","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ingrid Castellano is a hydrologist.</li><li>Castellano wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Castellano compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Castellano found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Castellano concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands, Castellano concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","Castellano concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","To investigate the question, Castellano compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Castellano found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.d84bd41d3e","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-95","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Sofia Quintero is a hydrologist.</li><li>Quintero wanted to find out whether wetlands reduce flooding downstream.</li><li>Quintero compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.</li><li>Quintero found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.</li><li>Quintero concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Quintero concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods.","Quintero found that river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands.","To investigate the question, Quintero compared river levels below restored wetlands with levels below drained farmland after storms.","Because river levels rose more slowly below the wetlands, Quintero concluded that wetlands may help protect nearby communities from floods."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.465eb837f3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-103","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Chen Delacroix is a chemist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Delacroix placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Delacroix found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Because most samples broke apart within four months, Delacroix concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Delacroix found that most samples broke apart within four months.","To investigate the question, Delacroix placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.ba37b0648c","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-104","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Jonas Duarte is a chemist.</li><li>Duarte wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Duarte placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Duarte found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Duarte concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Duarte concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","To investigate the question, Duarte placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Duarte found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Because most samples broke apart within four months, Duarte concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.d4ead772a0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-106","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Yara Brennan is a chemist.</li><li>Brennan wanted to find out whether a new plant-based plastic breaks down in seawater.</li><li>Brennan placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.</li><li>Brennan found that most samples broke apart within four months.</li><li>Brennan concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Brennan placed samples of the plastic in tanks of seawater for six months.","Brennan concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic.","Brennan found that most samples broke apart within four months.","Because most samples broke apart within four months, Brennan concluded that the plastic may be less harmful to oceans than conventional plastic."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.a0514aa3f7","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-108","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Leila Varga is a primatologist.</li><li>Varga wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Varga observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Varga found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Varga concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Varga concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","To investigate the question, Varga observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Because young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier, Varga concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","Varga found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.f8fc833fb2","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-109","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Petrov is a primatologist.</li><li>Petrov wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Petrov observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Petrov found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Petrov concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Petrov concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","Petrov found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","Because young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier, Petrov concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","To investigate the question, Petrov observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.01a2278a6a","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-113","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Delacroix is a primatologist.</li><li>Delacroix wanted to find out whether young chimpanzees learn to use tools by watching adults.</li><li>Delacroix observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.</li><li>Delacroix found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.</li><li>Delacroix concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Delacroix found that young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier.","To investigate the question, Delacroix observed young chimpanzees in groups where adults cracked nuts with stones and in groups where adults did not.","Delacroix concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation.","Because young chimpanzees in the nut-cracking groups began using stones much earlier, Delacroix concluded that young chimpanzees may learn tool use by observation."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.074a5e3325","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-115","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Ravi Novak is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Novak wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Novak asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Novak found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Novak concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Because tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep, Novak concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Novak concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","To investigate the question, Novak asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Novak found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep."],"answer":"A","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.0441fc4fe0","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-117","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Elias Rahman is a sleep researcher.</li><li>Rahman wanted to find out whether using screens before bed affects how quickly people fall asleep.</li><li>Rahman asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.</li><li>Rahman found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.</li><li>Rahman concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Rahman asked volunteers to read either a printed book or a tablet for an hour before bed.","Because tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep, Rahman concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep.","Rahman found that tablet readers took about ten minutes longer to fall asleep.","Rahman concluded that screen use before bed may delay sleep."],"answer":"B","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.a4b601b024","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-128","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Zara Moreau is a public health researcher.</li><li>Moreau wanted to find out whether adding bike lanes increases how often residents cycle.</li><li>Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.</li><li>Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year.</li><li>Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["To investigate the question, Moreau counted cyclists on streets before and after new bike lanes were added.","Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Because cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year, Moreau concluded that bike lanes may encourage more people to ride.","Moreau found that cycling on those streets nearly doubled within a year."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.63220d9590","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-152","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Kofi Abara is a climate scientist.</li><li>Abara wanted to find out whether light-colored roofs reduce indoor temperatures.</li><li>Abara compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.</li><li>Abara found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.</li><li>Abara concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Abara found that homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler.","To investigate the question, Abara compared indoor temperatures in homes with white roofs and homes with dark roofs.","Abara concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning.","Because homes with white roofs stayed several degrees cooler, Abara concluded that light-colored roofs may reduce the need for air-conditioning."],"answer":"D","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."},
{"id":"g.rw.synthesis.3.3780deeee3","section":"rw","domain":"expression","skill":"synthesis","difficulty":3,"group":"syn-s-165","passage":"<p>While researching a topic, a student has taken the following notes:</p><ul><li>Lucía Ferreira is a veterinary scientist.</li><li>Ferreira wanted to find out whether dogs recognize their owners' voices.</li><li>Ferreira played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.</li><li>Ferreira found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often.</li><li>Ferreira concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.</li></ul><p>The student wants to present both the study's finding and the conclusion drawn from it.</p>","prompt":"Which choice most effectively uses relevant information from the notes to accomplish this goal?","choices":["Ferreira concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","To investigate the question, Ferreira played recordings of owners' voices and strangers' voices to dogs.","Because dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often, Ferreira concluded that dogs may be able to tell their owners' voices apart from others.","Ferreira found that dogs turned toward their owners' voices far more often."],"answer":"C","explanation":"The goal has two parts, and only this choice includes both the finding and the conclusion. The others give only one part, or the method."}
